      "dcterms:title": "FROM STATE INTEGRALS TO q-SERIES",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "GAROUFALIDIS, STAVROS",
        "KASHAEV, RINAT"
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20170828",
      "dcterms:abstract": "It is well-known to the experts that multi-dimensional state integrals of prod- ucts of Faddeev’s quantum dilogarithm which arise in Quantum Topology can be written as ﬁnite sums of products of basic hypergeometric series in q = e2πiτ and ˜q = e−2πi/τ. We illustrate this fact by giving a detailed proof for a family of one-dimensional integrals which includes state-integral invariants of 41 and 52 knots.",
      "dcterms:source": "library/stateintegralsqseries/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/stateintegralsqseries"
    }
  ]
